Given a statement $\mathsf{s}$ and a consistent pair $(\Gamma, \Sigma)$ such that $\Gamma,\ell\vdash\mathsf{s}:\Gamma'$ and $\langle\Sigma,\mathsf{s}\rangle\Downarrow{\Sigma'}$ for some $\ell$, $\Gamma'$ and $\Sigma'$, then the following statements hold.
\begin{enumerate}
    \item If $\ell=\texttt{\#}\mathtt{t}$, then $\vert\Sigma'\vert\dot{-}\vert\Sigma\vert=O(\vert{(\Sigma)_{\restriction \Gamma}}\vert^d)$, where $d$ is a constant.
    \item If $\ell=\texttt{\#}\mathtt{f}$, then $\vert\Sigma'\vert\dot{-}\vert\Sigma\vert= O(\vert\Sigma\vert^{d^{k}})$, where $d$ and $k$ are constants.
\end{enumerate}

Given an expression $\mathsf{e}$ and a consistent pair $(\Gamma,\Sigma)$, if there exist $v$ and $\mathsf{t}$ such that $\langle\Sigma,\mathsf{e}\rangle\Downarrow{v}$ and $\Gamma,\texttt{\#}\mathtt{f}\vdash\mathsf{e}:\mathsf{t}$, then the following statements hold.
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $\vert v\vert\le\vert\Sigma\vert+k$, where $k$ is a constant.
    \item If $\mathsf{e}$ is iterable, i.e., $\mathsf{t}=\mathtt{iint}$, then $\vert v\vert\le\vert{(\Sigma)_{\restriction \Gamma}}\vert+k$, where $k$ is a constant.
\end{enumerate}
